{"name":"Buzzards Bay","hex":"#017a79","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Buzzards Bay","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A bay of the Atlantic Ocean, within the waters of southern Massachusetts, United States.","A census-designated place in the town of Bourne, Barnstable County, Massachusetts, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Buzzards_Bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Buzzards Bay","blocks":[{"text":"Buzzards Bay is a bay of the Atlantic Ocean adjacent to the U.S. state of Massachusetts. It is approximately 28 miles long by 8 miles wide. It is a popular destination for fishing, boating, and tourism. Buzzards Bay is often considered the finest sailing location on the East Coast and is frequently compared in terms of sailing conditions to San Francisco Bay. Since 1914, Buzzards Bay has been connected to Cape Cod Bay by the Cape Cod Canal. In 1988, under the Clean Water Act, the Environmental Protection Agency and the Commonwealth of Massachusetts designated Buzzards Bay to the National Estuary Program, as \"an estuary of national significance\" that is threatened by pollution, land development, or overuse."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Buzzards_Bay_map.png/330px-Buzzards_Bay_map.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buzzards_Bay","wikidata":"Q599732"},{"title":"Buzzards Bay (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Buzzards Bay is an American Thoroughbred racehorse."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buzzards_Bay_(horse)","wikidata":"Q5003576"},{"title":"Buzzard","blocks":[{"text":"Buzzard is the common name of several species of birds of prey."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buzzard","wikidata":"Q3251488"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay","wikidata":"Q39594"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Long_Island_from_space.jpg/500px-Long_Island_from_space.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Long_Island_from_space.jpg/500px-Long_Island_from_space.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Buzzards Bay and surrounding area from orbit (looking southwest)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALong_Island_from_space.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Buzzards_Bay%2C_Mass._%282673776441%29.jpg/500px-Buzzards_Bay%2C_Mass._%282673776441%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Buzzards_Bay%2C_Mass._%282673776441%29.jpg/1280px-Buzzards_Bay%2C_Mass._%282673776441%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Buzzards_Bay%2C_Mass._%282673776441%29.jpg/500px-Buzzards_Bay%2C_Mass._%282673776441%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Birds eye view map, 1909","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABuzz